  "cli.usage": "urftp — UltraRushFTP on the command line (site manager sites or URLs)\n\nUsage:\n  urftp sites                              list the sites of the site manager\n  urftp ls   <target>                      list a remote folder\n  urftp get  <target> [local folder]       download a file or a folder\n  urftp put  <file|folder> <target>        upload into the remote folder\n  urftp fxp  <source> <destination>        site-to-site transfer (FXP)\n  urftp raw  <site> <command>...           raw commands (FTP), replies printed\n\nTarget: \"SiteName:/path\" (site manager, case-insensitive name)\n        or URL \"ftp://user:pass@host:port/path\" (ftps://, ftpsi://, sftp://).\n\nOptions:\n  -v, --verbose          protocol log (password masked)\n  -n, --transfers <n>    simultaneous transfers per site (default: site setting)\n  --exists <action>      existing file: overwrite, resume, skip, rename\n  --insecure             accept any TLS certificate (FTPS)\n  --fingerprint <fp>     expected SHA-256 fingerprint (FTPS certificate or SFTP host key)\n  --data <folder>        settings folder (like -f of the interface)\n  --lang <en|fr>         language of the messages (default: Windows language)\n  -h, --help             this help",
